Injection points for the port's tests, at three of Apache Cloudberry's
faults inside a spill, which segspace and zlib in its regression tests
interrupt or fail (src/test/regress/sql):

  exec-hashjoin-new-batch    nodeHashjoin.c, ExecHashJoinNewBatch()  exec_hashjoin_new_batch
  workfile-creation-failure  buffile.c, BufFileCreateTemp()          workfile_creation_failure
  workfile-write-failure     buffile.c, BufFileDumpBuffer()          workfile_write_failure

gp_core's fault injector attaches a fault of Cloudberry's name to the point
(gp_fault.c).  Cloudberry asks for its write fault at each BufFileWrite();
this point is where the buffer is written out, once a block, so that the
tests' build looks for no attached point at each row a spill writes.  They
serve tests alone, so they are not in the core series: Dockerfile.pg
applies this after test-injection-points.patch, to the tree of either ref,
vanilla or patched, so that the two images still differ only in the ref.
Dormant, as any point is: without injection points the macro is empty, and
with them a point nothing attached to runs no callback.


